; Regression: a name that resolves to nothing, under a CAST (2026-09-28).
;
; `unknown_identifier_name#` judged a bare Type operand and answered "" for
; everything else, and a cast is a PlannedAs around the operand — so the
; operand under an `as` was never judged. Three shapes compiled at rc 0:
;
;   set seen: nosuchname as i64        the whole statement was DROPPED
;   print "`nosuchname as i64`"        printed an empty line
;   set x: current_task as size_t      a stdlib `mutable` global, which a
;                                      program cannot see: dropped too
;
; The third is how it was found: a scheduler test compared two such reads,
; both 0, and passed without measuring anything (ROADMAP-http.md, the
; spawn_detached gate). The first shape is pinned here; the neighbouring
; spellings `let p nosuchname` and `set seen: nosuchname` were loud already.
; xfail: unknown identifier: nosuchname

mutable seen: i64 7

procedure probe() mutable seen
{
    set seen: nosuchname as i64
    print "inside"
}

probe()
print "seen `seen`"
